1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:04,530
Welcome back to our lesson about meetings.

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:12,780
Last time we looked through the vocabulary that you will need during the meetings or to talk about meetings.

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,740
And in this part of the lesson, we will look at useful phrases.

4
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:21,870
So all of the phrases that you might want to use if you lead a meeting.

5
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:32,280
Starting with welcoming participants, apologies all the way through agenda points and summarizing what

6
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:35,880
we've decided and during the meeting and closing the meeting.

7
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:43,110
So this is just a bunch of phrases and we are going to differentiate between more formal and less formal

8
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,980
phrases and and sentences.

9
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:48,540
So let's dive into it.

10
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:56,520
Now, the first thing that you want to do when you start a meeting is you want to welcome attendees.

11
00:00:57,450 --> 00:01:02,640
A more formal way to do it is good morning and welcome everyone.

12
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:10,650
The purpose of today's meeting is to discuss and then you may introduce the main point of your meeting,

13
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:16,710
for example, to discuss ways to improve customer relations in all our branches.

14
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:22,290
So the text in the brackets here is just an example.

15
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:27,900
So you want to pay attention to this phrase in bold here.

16
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:29,380
Now.

17
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:33,040
You also may want to thank the attendees for coming.

18
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,590
So you may use a phrase

19
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,740
Thank you all for coming at such short notice.

20
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:48,370
At a short notice mean means that you haven't decided or arranged this meeting long ago

21
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:55,470
but for example, just a couple of days ago and the people came together to join the meeting.

22
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:59,200
So it was short notice, for example, a couple of days.

23
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:08,180
Now, if somebody is absent, you may want to give the apology so you can say, I have received apologies

24
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:15,230
for the absence of, for example, for the absence of Peter, who is on sick leave.

25
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:17,600
So these phrases are more formal.

26
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:22,280
If you have, for example, a team meeting, a regular team meeting.

27
00:02:22,670 --> 00:02:24,710
You don't want to be very formal.

28
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:27,260
So you say, hello, everyone.

29
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:28,550
Thank you for joining.

30
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:34,780
Now that everyone's here, let's get started with today's agenda, for example.

31
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:42,560
And to give apologies, you can simply say, unfortunately, Peter can't join today and you can give

32
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,700
a reason for that.

33
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,300
Now going on.

34
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:54,260
You will want to look at agenda and you want to introduce the objectives or the points in the agenda

35
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:56,660
so you can start like this.

36
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:00,680
We have a number of important matters on the agenda.

37
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,880
We are here today to discuss...

38
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:08,940
the changes to a project plan, for example.

39
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:14,840
First item on the agenda that we need to discuss today is...

40
00:03:15,610 --> 00:03:19,330
For example, increasing our cooperation on a global level.

41
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:25,810
Again, these phrases are more formal. If you have a less formal meeting

42
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:30,420
you can say, I've called this meeting in order to

43
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:32,530
So I've called the meeting.

44
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,290
It means that you organized the meeting.

45
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:42,490
So the first item on the agenda is, for example, the upcoming integration testing. Or

46
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:52,220
First, let's talk about... first, let's talk about how we can use social media to promote our new product.

47
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:54,230
Or

48
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:58,650
First, let's go over the minutes from our last meeting

49
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:02,730
which was held last Tuesday, for example.

50
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:11,760
So if you have a regular meeting and you do the meeting minutes every meeting, so it's good practice

51
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:18,540
to take the meeting minutes from the last meeting, go over them and see if you have any open tasks

52
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:25,140
or objectives or some points that you need to discuss or continue discussing.

53
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:31,110
So you can say, let's go over the meeting minutes from the last time.

54
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:41,370
Now, at some point in during the meeting, during the discussion, you may find yourself in the situation

55
00:04:41,370 --> 00:04:45,810
that you don't understand something or you don't fully understand something.

56
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:50,040
And there is a way to ask for clarification.

57
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:58,230
If you want to clarify something and you can say, Excuse me, can you please clarify what you said

58
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:00,180
about the merit increase process?

59
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:03,750
So to clarify to clarify means

60
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:04,770
to explain or 

61
00:05:04,770 --> 00:05:05,910
to elaborate.

62
00:05:05,910 --> 00:05:09,060
It's another interesting, more advanced word.

63
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,950
To elaborate on something.

64
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:15,090
It means to talk more, to give more details about something.

65
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,350
So clarify.

66
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:17,280
Explain.

67
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,120
Elaborate.

68
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:25,500
Some other ways to ask for clarifications, for example.

69
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:34,260
I'm not sure I understand what you mean by and you give your the problem that you want to get clarification

70
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:34,860
for.

71
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:41,550
For example, I'm not sure I understand what you mean by increasing the capacity of our delivery department.

72
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,590
Why you say

73
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,130
I'm not sure I understand,

74
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:53,870
it sounds more polite, and it sounds softer than if you just said, I don't understand.

75
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:59,250
So you give this introductory phrase.

76
00:05:59,270 --> 00:06:01,610
I'm not sure I understand.

77
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:07,520
And it makes it softer, especially if the situation if the meeting is very formal,

78
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:15,800
so you don't want to sound very like straightforward and maybe rude at some point that that's where

79
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,290
you want to use those phrases.

80
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:25,640
If it's a usual team meeting, you know, which has a well and you are on a first name basis, for example.

81
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:25,840
Yes.

82
00:06:25,850 --> 00:06:30,500
So you don't need to use those very formal introductory phrases.

83
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:36,620
Yeah, you can talk simpler, but if it's formal you may want to use those phrases.

84
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,210
I'm not sure I understand.

85
00:06:38,210 --> 00:06:43,250
And then you ask your question or you can say I'm sorry,

86
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:44,780
I don't quite follow.

87
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:46,780
For example.

88
00:06:46,810 --> 00:06:50,830
I'm sorry, I don't quite follow the calculation you are sharing right now.

89
00:06:51,910 --> 00:06:57,700
Again, the word quite makes the phrase softer, makes it more friendly.

90
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:58,770
Yeah.

91
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:04,000
You also can say I don't quite understand or I don't quite remember.

92
00:07:05,350 --> 00:07:13,330
So if somebody is talking about something that was discussed previously and you don't remember discussing

93
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:17,950
those things, you can say, I'm sorry, I don't quite remember

94
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:19,270
we discussed this.

95
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:26,620
So this quite, the word quite means makes it softer, more friendly, more polite.

96
00:07:28,150 --> 00:07:34,270
Now at some point you want to bring up a new point in the conversation.

97
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:36,700
Phrases to do that.

98
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:41,290
Before we move on, I think we need to look at

99
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:53,110
So when the agenda topics is changing and the chair of the meeting is going on to another point,

100
00:07:53,110 --> 00:08:00,010
but you want to stop at this point and discuss something else, something additional. In this in this

101
00:08:00,010 --> 00:08:06,490
case, you can say Before we move on, I think we need to look at, for example, how we can ensure

102
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:09,160
that it will not happen during the next sprint.

103
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:09,720
Yeah.

104
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:16,810
So you want to discuss the problem in more detail before we move before you move to some other topics.

105
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:20,020
Another phrase you can use.

106
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:23,860
I'm sorry, but I don't believe we've talked about

107
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:28,660
I'm sorry, but I don't believe we've talked about.. Again

108
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:30,160
I don't believe.

109
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:34,080
This is the softener. 

110
00:08:34,179 --> 00:08:34,289
Yeah.

111
00:08:34,309 --> 00:08:39,679
This is something that makes the phrase seem more polite.

112
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:40,970
Sound more polite,

113
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:41,240
yeah.

114
00:08:43,059 --> 00:08:44,049
Another phrase.

115
00:08:44,049 --> 00:08:45,230
One minute, please,

116
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:48,930
it seems we haven't discussed something.

117
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:52,750
One minute it seems we haven't discussed.. Again 

118
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:59,590
you give the phrase "it seems that we haven't discussed" to make it softer and more polite.

119
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:10,800
Now at some point you want to move on, especially if you are not a participant of the meeting, but

120
00:09:10,950 --> 00:09:19,200
leader of the meeting, for example, a project manager or a team leader, and you lead and you conduct

121
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,160
the whole meeting.

122
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:27,900
So at some point you can see that the discussion is going into a lot of the detail and maybe you don't

123
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,960
need to discuss everything at this meeting.

124
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:38,190
You can leave it for some other time because you have other things on your agenda and you want to ask

125
00:09:38,190 --> 00:09:43,920
people to leave it at that and move to the next agenda point.

126
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:53,160
So for this, you can simply say Let's move on to.., for example, let's move on to the status of our

127
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,390
ongoing project.

128
00:09:55,410 --> 00:10:00,660
Or you can say, moving on, let's take a look at item three on the agenda.

129
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:06,900
And then you introduce this item.

130
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:12,640
Or you can say Now we've come to the final item on the agenda

131
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:15,490
For example, our new marketing campaign.

132
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:23,950
So at some point you may want to stop people and stop discussing some point and you want to move to

133
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:25,930
another point to the next point.

134
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:28,750
And here you use those phrases.

135
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:29,890
Moving on.

136
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:35,210
Okay, givning control.

137
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:42,980
If you lead the meeting, you conduct the meeting, and you have a lot of the things to introduce and

138
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,240
to discuss, that's good.

139
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:51,280
But at some point you may not be the expert in a particular area or a particular topic.

140
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:59,720
And in this case, you want to give the control to somebody else to ask someone else to speak on the

141
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:02,660
topic or to lead this discussion.

142
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,520
How you can do this.

143
00:11:05,090 --> 00:11:06,470
Let's look at the phrases.

144
00:11:07,430 --> 00:11:15,170
Jane, would you like to kick off? or would you like to introduce the first item on the today's agenda?

145
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:18,170
So kick off means to start.

146
00:11:18,170 --> 00:11:21,290
Would you like to start discussing this point?

147
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:24,140
Another one.

148
00:11:25,190 --> 00:11:32,850
I'd like to hand over to, I'd like to hand over to Thomas, who is going to talk about blah, blah.

149
00:11:33,770 --> 00:11:43,340
So to hand over means that you ask the person to speak about something, to introduce a topic, or to

150
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:47,870
give their opinion on something yet to hand over.

151
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:53,880
Or you can simply say Okay, Martin, over to you.

152
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:59,310
Over to you means you give them control of the discussion.

153
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:04,930
Another phrase Victoria, could you please comment on that?

154
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:07,330
Could you please comment on that?

155
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:11,790
You have a colleague in the meeting and you want their input.

156
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:17,560
You want them to say or to add something on the topic that you are discussing.

157
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:21,870
So this is how you try to invite the person to the conversation.

158
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,860
Could you please comment on that?

159
00:12:24,690 --> 00:12:28,470
Or Maria, could you please share your thoughts? Again

160
00:12:28,470 --> 00:12:36,030
you are inviting somebody, someone specific to share their thoughts or to comment on something, to

161
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:37,680
add some new information.

162
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:40,290
Okay.

163
00:12:40,310 --> 00:12:40,850
Good.

164
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:49,850
Now, coming to the closing point of the meeting of the discussion, you want sometimes you want to

165
00:12:49,850 --> 00:13:00,260
summarize the discussion, so that everybody who participated in the meeting knows what we've decided

166
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:04,580
on, what we want to do and what we've agreed on.

167
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:06,650
So how to summarize?

168
00:13:07,610 --> 00:13:07,940
Here

169
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:12,380
you can say In summary, we're going to do the following

170
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:19,220
And you say what you've what you've decided on during the meeting.

171
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:23,210
For example, in summary, we are going to do the following.

172
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:27,440
Jane will contact our suppliers and Thomas will prepare the paperwork.

173
00:13:29,150 --> 00:13:30,230
Another phrase.

174
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,880
This is what we've agreed on.

175
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:42,580
And again, you give you summarize, you give the summary, and then you can add, for example, we

176
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:47,050
will meet in a week and synchronize on the progress.

177
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:56,260
To synchronize means we will each say what we have done and we will see at what level we are, what

178
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,320
is our progress.

179
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:00,100
So we will synchronize our progress.

180
00:14:00,850 --> 00:14:09,040
And the last phrase here We've decided on.. very simple phrase to summarize at the end of the meeting,

181
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:15,490
We have decided on fixed price as a type of our supply contracts, for example, or anything else.

182
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:20,560
And the last thing is how to close the meeting.

183
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:28,510
Closing the meeting. A more formal way is to say the meeting is adjourned, the meeting is adjourned.

184
00:14:28,510 --> 00:14:30,760
It means it's closed.

185
00:14:31,210 --> 00:14:35,320
Thank you all for attending. And a less formal way,

186
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,450
of course, there can be a variety of ways

187
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,890
how to close the meeting.

188
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:42,730
I guess that's all for today or just That's all for today.

189
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:46,810
Thank you for coming. Or That's all for today.

190
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,820
Have a nice rest of the day, everyone.

191
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:55,600
So you kind of say your goodbyes and wish people a nice day or nice weekend or whatever.

192
00:14:57,010 --> 00:15:02,980
So these were the phrases on how to move around in the meeting, how to lead a meeting.

193
00:15:03,730 --> 00:15:05,740
I hope that was useful for you.

194
00:15:06,430 --> 00:15:08,350
Do the quiz. See in the next one.

